From 40dbbaf4c80ab4b7a7c6c26f09ca500c85162891 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: windy <windy325799@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 22:38:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ai): enhance SQL AI functions for the competition task

Implement the six AI function enhancement items required by the
2026-competition task on top of the existing AI_PROMPT/AI_COMPLETE/
AI_EMBED/AI_RERANK implementation:

- AI_PROMPT: accept CHAR/VARCHAR/BINARY/TEXT/BLOB/LONGTEXT templates and
  JSON arguments, keep JSON array/object arguments structured, support
  nested prompt objects, {{ and }} escapes, repeated placeholders and
  strict rejection of malformed or out-of-range placeholders.
- AI_EMBED: accept text/lob content, return LONGTEXT JSON, validate the
  explicit dimension and the returned vector shape, propagate NULL input
  as NULL, and evaluate table scans in cross-row batches with bounded
  request size and order-preserving result mapping.
- AI_COMPLETE: accept AI_PROMPT objects and JSON/string config, ignore a
  NULL config, and reject empty or non-string model responses.
- Ollama provider: allow an empty access key, match providers
  case-insensitively, implement the native /api/generate and /api/embed
  protocol (stream=false, options mapping) and response validation.
- AI_RERANK: normalize provider results per batch (every input index
  present, stable ordering by score then original position), remap
  batched indices to global positions, and validate the final result
  before sorting the original documents.

Ref #1544
